    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6b4b5bda-5fd6-59b2-aa38-674bcc51785d",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 25\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 65\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -65\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=40 \\\\ y &=-65\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-65$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\left(-65\\right)=40\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=40+65=105.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=105$ and $y=-65.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
