      ":question/id": "1b0a048f-affc-52e3-b9de-7d1eee06b971",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 10 & -40\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 10 & -40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=-10 \\\\ y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=5$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7\\left(5\\right)=-10\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=-10-35=-45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-45$ and $y=5.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
